        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https://www.autohotkey.com/\">AutoHotkey (AHK)</a> is a free and simple yet powerful Windows scripting language. It doesn\u2019t get a lot of press these days, but Windows geeks used to love writing and swapping AHK scripts.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>You can learn AHK and write the scripts yourself if you want to\u2014the <a href=\"https://www.autohotkey.com/docs/v2/\">AutoHotkey documentation is pretty good</a>\u2014or you could use an AI tool like <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/\">ChatGPT</a>, <a href=\"https://gemini.google.com/\">Gemini</a>, <a href=\"https://claude.ai/\">Claude</a>, <a href=\"https://copilot.microsoft.com/\">Copilot</a>, etc. to do the work for you.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Well, that\u2019s what I did. Months ago, I vibe-coded <a href=\"https://www.computerworld.com/article/3962792/a-better-way-to-scroll-in-windows.html\">a script that changes how scrolling works on Windows</a>. (Vibe codi",
